            <div xml:id="d153">

                <pb facs="0263" n="145" sameAs="frus:frus1929v03/pg145"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">314.115C43/148: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Guatemala</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Geissler</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Guatemala</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-08-08T17:00:00-06:00">August 8, 1929—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 9:43 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>102. Referring to the Department’s telegram of August 7, 2 p.m. The Minister for
                    Foreign Affairs orally joined in the selection of the Chief Justice of British
                    Honduras and agrees that he sit at Belize.</p>
                <p>The Minister suggests that the Department and the Guatemalan Minister in
                    Washington ascertain through the British Embassy whether the Chief Justice
                    accepts. He suggests that if the Chief <pb facs="0264" n="146" xml:id="pg146"/>
                    Justice does not accept some Cuban could perhaps be agreed upon because of
                    proximity.</p>
                <p>The Minister agrees that a decision regarding the honorarium be deferred.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Geissler</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
